  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India: the Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy, MPC resolutions and minutes, the monthly release on Lending and Deposit Rates of Scheduled Commercial Banks, the Weekly Statistical Supplement, auction results, and the Database on Indian Economy (DBIE), all read from India Atlas's archived copy of these RBI publications. CPI from MoSPI, read from this site's CPI guide. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={N["prov-vintage"]}></b>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Policy rates are carried forward from each change to give the level on any date. Amounts are converted from rupees to ₹ crore. Where a table prints one value per display unit, only the actual values are read. Weighted averages, sums by financial year, real rates and the term spread are India Atlas calculations, labelled as such. Nothing is estimated; impossible printed values (a negative tenor or rate) are left empty and listed.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Separate rulers are never joined: the Bank Rate and the repo rate; the reverse repo and the SDF as the floor; benchmark lending rates (base rate, MCLR, external benchmark); the annual lending-rate tables to 2014 and the monthly release from 2012; deposit rates of all banks to 1999-00 and of five major banks from 2000-01; CPI on the 2012 and 2024 bases.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026. Revised after each MPC meeting and each monthly lending-rate release.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
